cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnimalTaskSim in your research, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "AnimalTaskSim: Testing Explanations of Animal Decisions Against Trial-Level Behavioral Data"
authors:
  - family-names: Akar
    given-names: Erman
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-02-19"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ermanakar/animaltasksim"
abstract: >
  AnimalTaskSim provides task environments, comparison agents, schema-validated
  trial logs, and a shared evaluation pipeline for testing explanations of
  animal choices against trial-level behavioral data. Explanations are compared
  by held-out prediction on source-verified mouse and macaque reference data,
  with frozen protocols and model-recovery checks. Hybrid drift-diffusion and
  recurrent agents are retained as comparison models, not validated mechanisms.
keywords:
  - decision making
  - choice history
  - model comparison
  - drift diffusion model
  - recurrent neural networks
  - IBL mice
  - macaque
  - psychophysics

